# Parcego Merchant Landing Page – UI Implementation Rule

## Objective

Build a visually premium, conversion-focused landing page for Parcego, targeting merchants, using only the provided design tokens and style guide. The page must be as visually compelling and merchant-centric as Stallion’s, but with Parcego’s unique value, branding, and accessibility standards.

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only (no custom CSS)
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **Design Tokens:** Use only the provided color, font, spacing, border, and shadow tokens.
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions (see below).
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast).

---

## 2. Page Structure & Content

### Hero Section
- Parcego SVG logo (merchant version, prominent)
- Headline: Large, bold, merchant-focused
- Subheadline: Short, benefit-driven
- Primary CTA: “Get Started Free” (primary button)
- Secondary CTA: “See How It Works” (secondary button)
- Clean background, subtle accent or illustration

### Feature Highlights
- 3–4 cards, each with icon, title, and description
- Use card tokens for styling

### How It Works
- 3–4 step process, each with icon/illustration and text

### Rate Calculator (Mock)
- Simple form: From, To, Package type, Weight, Dimensions
- “Get Estimate” button (mock result)
- Show sample rate and delivery time

### Testimonials/Trust
- 2–3 merchant testimonials (mock)
- Supported platform logos

### Comparison Banner
- “Why Parcego vs. Stallion?” (short, factual)
- Table or bullet points: Parcego advantages

### Call to Action (Footer)
- Main CTA: “Join Parcego Free”
- Secondary links: Contact, Support, Terms, Privacy

---

## 3. Design & Implementation Rules

- **Brand Colors:** Use only tokens (primary: #007bff, dark: #0056b3, etc.)
- **Typography:** Use only provided font families, sizes, and weights.
- **Spacing:** Use only provided spacing tokens.
- **Buttons:** Use component tokens for primary/secondary.
- **Cards:** Use card tokens for background, radius, shadow.
- **Accessibility:** All elements must have ARIA labels, keyboard navigation, and color contrast compliance.
- **Responsiveness:** Mobile-first, fully responsive.
- **Transitions:** Use only transform: scale, opacity, color, and shadow for hover/active states. **Do not use translateY(-2px) on hover.** Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- **No dead code, no TODOs, no placeholders.**
- **All IDs and classes must use the `parcego-` prefix and follow the global naming rules.**
- **All icons must be rendered as `<span>` with kebab-case classes and data-icon attributes.**
- **No Shopify-specific flows or forms.**

---

## 4. Accessibility & Testing

- All interactive elements must be accessible by keyboard and screen reader.
- All color contrast must meet WCAG AA.
- All forms must have proper labels and error states.
- Test with reduced motion enabled.

---

## 5. Deliverables

- Complete landing page at `/` (or `/landing` if `/` is reserved)
- All components and assets (SVG logo, icons, etc.)
- README update with run instructions

---

## 6. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify strict adherence to this rule file and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern merchant landing page for Parcego, ready for future backend/API integration, and visually superior to Stallion’s offering.